title The room next door had held this reading for twelve days
prompt the standing autonomous loop -- take the next agent-doable lap in the amphora and bron-resins lane
rota lap 4223, row 3 -- Water, the row that tastes: care and flow, read up close. It sent me to read the actual files rather than the counts written about them, which is how the drift surfaced.
rota lap 4226, row 1 -- Air, the row that feels: law and boundary, read on the recovery lap. Air's sense is touch, and touch only works at a surface -- which is what this lap's instrument does, pressing on the claim that every module has a guard and naming where the hand passes through.
think Cold roster open GREEN -- 177 guards, 174 green, 0 red, 3 gated, 1313s. No red books the allocation, so the lap is constructive.
think Opened on %360's question in my own lane: does any Amphora witness stand off the roster? Five do -- amphora_device_wire, lap1, lap2, vessel_seal, vessel_stamp, all accrete shims onto tools/gen/amphora/.
think Ran all five rather than reading about them. Four GREEN at 1s each; amphora_device_wire refuses, and the cause is this pier holding no qemu-system-riscv64 rather than any Amphora fault.
think The roster block already names and declines all five by name, with reasons -- so the discipline held and my find was already answered. Reading it is what kept me from rostering four guards against a stated decision.
think Beside that decision stood drift nobody was reading: amphora/README.md claims twelve standing witnesses run every lap; the roster carries 15 rows under tools/am/, 13 on the lap clock, 8 asserting a refusal.
think tools/fixtures/t/tally_roster_scan.sh has asked the same coverage question of tally/ since 20260826. The vessel room answered it in prose for twelve days after, because a good pattern announces nothing.
think Built the instrument rather than retyping the number: room read with find ! -type l so a symlink is another lane's module, roster read for rows under the guard room, a shim followed one hop bounded at four.
obs Coverage is measured against the ROSTER, not against tools/. A witness that exists and is unrostered guards nothing (%360), and the control's fourth leg plants exactly that: a witness naming a module, no row, module still UNCOVERED.
obs singly_covered is reported and never gated. A module born today is named by exactly one guard on the day it lands, so a ceiling there would red on the most ordinary work in the room.
obs REDS.md stood 14 bytes under its ceiling, so booking cost a fold. Folded my own BOOKED %591 to a shelf, booked %595, folded it CLOSED in the same lap -- the pin keeps what is open.
obs The card is held tight too: fitting this lap's account under 40,960 took seven passes of trimming. A living pin at its ceiling taxes every lap a judgment call, exactly as the baton says.
obs FIFTH PARK, AND THE FIRST RECOVERED INSIDE ONE HOUR. The whole lap above -- 592 insertions across 15 files, witness green and control 40/0 -- sat in stash@{0}, parked by the round-open at 20260907.232003 before it could commit. %499 has now cost this ship two laps and the fleet at least six.
obs Recovery split by peer-touch exactly as the fourth park taught. Three conflicts, all in shared pins, none in my own new files: README.md's metrics block (took HEAD's 1873; the hook regenerates it), REDS-fold-recital.md (accretion, both sides kept in stamp order), and REDS.md.
obs The REDS.md conflict was the one that needed a judgment rather than a merge. HEAD already carried %592 and %591 on the pin; my stash's version was the OLDER file with %587 still pinned. Taking either side whole would have been a rollback, so I took HEAD and re-applied only my own act on it -- deleting the %591 row whose fold shelf this lap ships. A snapshot of a shared file is a rollback; an act re-applied to the current file is a merge.
obs Fetched before trusting the numbers: reds_spine_derive reads shared_max=594, local_max=595, rebindings=0, squatters=0, next_free=596 -- so %595 is mine and unshared, and the recovery moved no published number.
obs What made this recovery cheap was that the parked work was already whole: witness, control, roster row, door page, ledger fold and log all committed to the stash together. A park costs a lap; a park of a HALF-lap would cost the work.
