obs THIS LOG LANDED THREE HOURS AFTER IT WAS WRITTEN, at 20260908.031128, and two of its file fields named paths that never got written because the lap was parked before it could commit. The shelf this lap would have made for its elder account is one of them: the live front folded on without it, so no such file exists and the line naming it is withdrawn rather than invented. The other two are repointed above to the shelves that actually carry those rows.
scope one keystone recovered -- the vessel room's coverage instrument, its roster row, the door page it corrects, and one ledger row folded
status GREEN -- amphora_roster witness green on metal after recovery (40 behaviors, 0 failed), scan verdict=ok with uncovered=0 and orphan_rows=0, exec_bit ok, reds_spine_derive ok on the fetched spine. Recovered whole from stash@{0}; three shared-pin conflicts resolved by re-applying my own act rather than snapshotting a peer's file.
recommend keep-going -- carry the same scan to mantra/, caravan/ or comlink/, one witness and one roster row each, each in its own lane
